*.muxa-backup-*
*.muxa-popup-*

# Cloudflare Wrangler
worker/.wrangler/

# The global ~/.gitignore excludes *.manifest, which silently dropped this file
# from a commit until a restore rehearsal caught it. It is generated state we
# deliberately track: without it install.sh cannot rebuild the skill farm. Only
# skills from the public agent-skills repo are listed; private ones are restored
# from their own repo and must not be catalogued here.
!configs/claude/skills.manifest

# Any Claude session whose project root is $HOME writes its memories straight
# into configs/claude/memory (that path is the symlink target), so files land
# here without review. This repo is public. The memories committed deliberately
# stay tracked — .gitignore does not apply to tracked files — while anything new
# needs `git add -f`, which is the review step.
configs/claude/memory/*.md

# skill-index SKILL.md and triggers.json are generated from the live skill tree,
# so they name every private skill installed on the machine. build.py stays
# tracked and rebuilds them locally; categories.json holds the private labels.
configs/claude/skill-index/SKILL.md
configs/claude/skill-index/triggers.json
configs/claude/skill-index/categories.json

# MEMORY.md is the memory index: one line per memory, written automatically by
# every session. The per-memory files above are ignored, but a tracked index
# leaks the same content through their summaries, bypassing the add -f review.
configs/claude/memory/MEMORY.md
